---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import FloatingCTA from '../../components/FloatingCTA.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "How Much Auto Insurance Do You Really Need in Mississippi?",
  "description": "A comprehensive guide to Mississippi auto insurance requirements, state minimums vs recommended limits, and why Uninsured Motorist coverage is essential in MS.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Melanee Pinion"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "InsuranceAgency",
    "name": "Pinion Family Insurance",
    "url": "https://pinionfamilyinsurance.com"
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-01-15",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-01"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much Auto Insurance Do You Really Need in Mississippi? | Pinion Family Insurance"
  description="Learn about Mississippi auto insurance minimums (25/50/25), recommended liability limits (100/300/100), and why Uninsured Motorist coverage is vital in Oxford, MS."
  schema={articleSchema}
>
  <Header />

  <article class="article-detail-page">
    <header class="article-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="article-hero-content">
          <a href="/resources" class="back-link">← Back to Resource Center</a>
          <span class="article-badge">Auto Insurance Guide</span>
          <h1>How Much Auto Insurance Do You Really Need in Mississippi?</h1>
          <div class="article-meta-bar">
            <span>By <strong>Melanee Pinion</strong></span>
            <span>·</span>
            <span>Independent Agent, Oxford MS</span>
            <span>·</span>
            <span>6 min read</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container article-container">
      <div class="article-layout">
        <div class="article-content">
          <p class="lead-text">
            If you drive in Oxford, Lafayette County, or anywhere in Mississippi, the law requires you to carry basic liability insurance. But there is a massive gap between what the state legally requires and what you actually need to protect your family's savings, home, and assets after a serious highway collision.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Mississippi State Minimum Requirements (25/50/25)</h2>
          <p>
            Under Mississippi law, every registered vehicle must maintain at least the following bodily injury and property damage liability limits:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>$25,000 Bodily Injury Liability</strong> per person injured in an accident you cause.</li>
            <li><strong>$50,000 Bodily Injury Liability</strong> total per accident (regardless of how many people are hurt).</li>
            <li><strong>$25,000 Property Damage Liability</strong> for damage to other vehicles or structures.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="callout-box warning-box">
            <h4>⚠️ Why 25/50/25 Leaves You at Severe Financial Risk</h4>
            <p>
              The average new truck or SUV in Mississippi costs over $50,000. If you accidentally rear-end a late-model vehicle and total it, a $25,000 property limit leaves a $25,000+ shortfall that you are personally responsible for paying out of pocket. Worse, if someone requires emergency trauma surgery or overnight ICU care at Baptist Memorial Hospital-North Mississippi, a $25,000 injury cap will be exhausted within hours.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2>2. Recommended Coverage: 100/300/100</h2>
          <p>
            For homeowners, working parents, and individuals with accumulated savings or real estate, standard practice among trusted independent agents is carrying:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>$100,000</strong> per person bodily injury</li>
            <li><strong>$300,000</strong> per accident bodily injury</li>
            <li><strong>$100,000</strong> property damage</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Upgrading from state minimums to 100/300/100 typically costs surprisingly little — often just <strong>$15 to $30 more per month</strong> when bundled with homeowners insurance.
          </p>

          <h2>3. The Uninsured Motorist Epidemic in Mississippi</h2>
          <p>
            According to national insurance industry studies, Mississippi consistently ranks among the top states for uninsured drivers — with nearly <strong>29% of motorists carrying zero auto insurance</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Uninsured/Underinsured Motorist (UM/UIM) Coverage</strong> protects you and your passengers if you are hit by a hit-and-run driver or someone with no coverage. We strongly advise carrying UM limits equal to your primary liability limits.
          </p>

          <h2>4. Comprehensive vs. Collision Coverage</h2>
          <p>
            In North Mississippi, vehicle claims frequently involve non-crash hazards:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Comprehensive:</strong> Covers deer strikes on rural Lafayette County roads, hailstorm body damage, windshield cracks, and fallen tree branches during spring thunderstorms.</li>
            <li><strong>Collision:</strong> Covers damage when your car hits another vehicle, a ditch, or an object, regardless of fault.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="guide-cta-box">
            <h3>Get a Fast, Custom Quote Comparison</h3>
            <p>At Pinion Family Insurance, we shop 15+ top carriers (Progressive, Travelers, Safeco, Nationwide, etc.) to get you maximum coverage at lower monthly rates.</p>
            <div class="cta-actions">
              <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Compare Auto Rates Now</a>
              <a href="tel:+16626383777" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Call (662) 638-3777</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="article-sidebar">
          <div class="sidebar-widget">
            <h4>Quick Summary</h4>
            <ul class="summary-list">
              <li><strong>MS State Minimum:</strong> 25/50/25</li>
              <li><strong>Recommended:</strong> 100/300/100</li>
              <li><strong>Uninsured Rate:</strong> ~29% in MS</li>
              <li><strong>Must-Have Add-on:</strong> UM/UIM + Comp</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="sidebar-widget agent-widget">
            <img src="/images/PFI-logo-small.webp" alt="Pinion Family Insurance" width="60" height="60" />
            <h5>Pinion Family Insurance</h5>
            <p>2621A W Oxford Loop<br/>Oxford, MS 38655</p>
            <a href="tel:+16626383777" class="phone-sidebar">(662) 638-3777</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
  <FloatingCTA />
</BaseLayout>

